1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,384
My landlord doesn't want my rent money. He demands my very best childhood memories instead.

2
00:00:06,684 --> 00:00:14,004
He sits across my kitchen table every single month, holding a glass jar that glows with golden light.

3
00:00:14,304 --> 00:00:20,376
Inside that glass swirls the exact afternoon my father taught me how to ride a red bicycle.

4
00:00:20,676 --> 00:00:28,188
I hand it over willingly because the alternative is much worse. Eviction means forgetting completely.

5
00:00:28,488 --> 00:00:34,320
Today the ledger was empty. I had no joy left to give him for this month's shelter.

6
00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:41,988
He smiled warmly and tapped my forehead. Don't worry, my child, we can manufacture a brand new one.

7
00:00:42,288 --> 00:00:49,704
A sudden flash of a summer beach filled my mind. Golden sun, laughing parents, endless warmth.

8
00:00:50,004 --> 00:00:56,748
It felt so real, so vivid. But as I reached for the memory, the edges began to burn away.

9
00:00:57,048 --> 00:01:04,824
The beach vanished, revealing grey concrete walls underneath. I had never even learned to ride a bike.

10
00:01:05,124 --> 00:01:09,540
If your happiest days were rented, who were you before you moved in?
